<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila virilis Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 3.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Module docstring states the scale, the age, and which species changes a. steady_state, onset_k2, and sigma_of_k are the textbook objects. Lean theorems restate the ordering the script checks by rounding nanometres. The render composite is labeled as a modulation, not as a derivation of the veins." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila virilis Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 3.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Schnakenberg steady state, Jacobian, onset k_c, and the four Turing inequalities are the published relations, and Du is solved from that onset law so virilis sits at 3.101 µm. The 2D field is explicit Euler on a fixed periodic patch. The chronospecies split is a change in a at fixed Du, which is a reconstruction, not a measured diffusivity. Deduction for the fixed domain and for using the habitus only as a modulated photograph rather than as the PDE domain." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila virilis Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 3.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Linearized growth rates on the real-eigenvalue band correlate with continuum σ(k) at Pearson r = 0.998 (RMSE 0.032), above the 0.98 threshold and not equal to it. Emergent midline spacing is 3.625 µm against the 3.101 µm onset reference. Habitus Nyquist is 7.76 µm. Orientation KS and pixel Pearson are computed against the photograph and are not copied from the reference anchors. Single specimen; a is not an independent empirical series." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-ablation-to-wild-type-activator-std-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-ks-statistic-of-gradient-orientation-specimen-versus-adult-endpoint>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-pearson-r-of-numerical-versus-analytic-dispersion-sigma-k>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-pixel-pearson-r-of-adult-endpoint-versus-specimen-habitus>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-rmse-of-dispersion-sigma-k>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-foreground-fraction>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-habitus-nyquist-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-specimen-structure-tensor-coherency>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-teissieri-onset-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-virilis-emergent-midline-peak-spacing>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-virilis-onset-wavelength-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-virilis-tergite-mode-count>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-measurement-willistoni-selected-wavelength>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila virilis Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 3.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 86.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 1. Shared Du and Dv/Du = 10, species-specific basal activator a. Onset wavelength is 3.101 µm for D. virilis (a = 0.10), 2.924 µm for predecessor D. teissieri (a = 0.058, still unstable), and no selected wavenumber for successor D. willistoni (a = 0.360, discriminant negative). All three are Holocene (0 Ma). Linearized dispersion Pearson r = 0.998 against continuum σ(k) (RMSE 0.032). Equal-diffusion ablation quenches activator std from 0.043 to 0. Saturated midline spacing is 3.625 µm, not the onset value. The Hanson 2019 habitus has a Nyquist length of 7.76 µm and does not resolve 3.1 µm. Overall 86.3/100 (faithfulness 85.6, reproducibility 88.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0c76d15d; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 88, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_virilis_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0c76d15d, image/png, 564225 B, 1512×984 px, artifact_sha256 f27ebb8d2c1a036dbe5cbd86236a8e9d7ea71a9116efe3980ac1f95b7da69d5e (sha256 f27ebb8d2c1a036dbe5cbd86236a8e9d7ea71a9116efe3980ac1f95b7da69d5e), spec_fingerprint 7b617b1b25587059791fa537573c287d828ce4628df471d7ad0d187921f12af8. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 7b617b1b25587059791fa537573c287d828ce4628df471d7ad0d187921f12af8; artifact_sha256: f27ebb8d2c1a036dbe5cbd86236a8e9d7ea71a9116efe3980ac1f95b7da69d5e. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical-wavenumber selection from the dispersion relation of a two-species reaction-diffusion system. | Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics and the steady state u0 = a + b, v0 = b/(a+b)^2. | Gompel et al. 2005: abdominal pigment differences among Drosophila species are cis-regulatory, including posterior bands in the melanogaster subgroup. | Hanson 2019 CC BY-SA 4.0 lateral habitus of Drosophila virilis (Wikimedia File:Dvir 1-2.jpg).; reconstructed_in_script: Du solved so virilis onset λ_c = 3.101 µm at Dv/Du = 10 and b = 0.90. | Teissieri a = 0.058 and willistoni a = 0.360 as the chronoseries step at fixed age and fixed diffusivities. | Tergite mode counts from project atlas adult lengths divided by seven. | Adult GIF endpoint is the habitus photograph modulated by the normalized PDE field.; transfer_boundary: The 3.101 µm target is the slot scale. It is not a published ocellus measurement for D. virilis. | Atlas body lengths are used only to turn a wavelength into a mode count.; does_not_claim: That the habitus photograph resolves a 3.1 µm pigment wavelength (measured Nyquist is 7.76 µm). | That willistoni lost a Turing pattern through geological time (successor is extant, 0 Ma). | That chorion-filament number enters the wavenumber law. | That the PDE generated the wing veins or the body outline.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "open need [model_equation/model-fidelity, pressure P=5.0]: Fixed 48 by 32 µm patch. No growing ocellar disc, so mode insertion with domain length is not demonstrated.",
        "open need [specimen_comparison/morphometric-validation, pressure P=3.0]: One lateral habitus. Pixel scale cannot confirm the 3.101 µm mode.",
        "remediation needed: R1. The PDE lives on a fixed 48 by 32 µm patch. Add a domain-length series and show that the number of activator peaks increases with patch length (mode count), which this pass does not measure.",
        "remediation needed: R2. The Hanson habitus Nyquist length is 7.76 µm. Keep that as an explicit negative result: the photograph is not evidence for the 3.101 µm wavelength.",
        "remediation needed: R3. Basal activator levels are reconstructed from pigmentation class. They are not a fit to a measured virilis concentration series.",
        "remediation needed: R4. Scores are from one assessor." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.63e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila virilis Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 3.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Onset wavelength increases monotonically with basal activator a on [0.06, 0.12]. Equal diffusion (Dv = Du) drops activator standard deviation from 0.043 to 0. Teissieri, virilis, and willistoni are the same Du and Dv at three values of a, and only the first two are unstable. The diffusion ratio itself is not swept." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila virilis Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 3.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Reproducibility package: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic seed 3210, --self-test covers the wavelength ordering, the quench, Pearson r > 0.98, ablation, monotonicity, Nyquist, and the pinned SHA-256. One command renders the PNG and the 12-frame GIF. No dependency lock beyond the repository requirements file. Single-assessor scores." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-repro-package-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-virilis-turing-wavelength-s0-source-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila virilis Schnakenberg onset wavelength at 3.1 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — Source and data traceability: 90/100" ;
